  "scope_note": "Pins BATCH-a51f91 before independent review. UNREVIEWED. No ML-KEM break, no security proof, no FIPS 203 parameter set affected or cleared, no speedup, no exponent moved. The mechanism studied is SESSION recovery, not key recovery, and no number here is subtracted from the in-repo primal_bdd margins of 2.80/6.04/1.28 bits. Rule 12 UNMET and UNWAIVED.",
  "producer_outcomes_pending_review": {
    "T1_census": "14 deployment-mode rows: 6 fix M = 1, 8 state NO COUNT BOUND at all; the largest numeric M stated by any of 24 rows, ephemeral or static, is 1. The producer explicitly DECLINED to read this as a ceiling: none of the 8 count-unstated modes forbids a large M either, so the absence is an absence in BOTH directions. Every static row bounds the key in TIME or by a rate-limiting SHOULD, never by a count, and the one normative count delegation (draft-ietf-tls-hybrid-design-16 Sec. 2) dead-ends at FIPS 203, which states no such bound by negative full-text search. CNSA 2.0 unretrieved, 403 x3, recorded as an acquisition failure under rule 5.",
    "T4_reads": "KILL (iii) DOES NOT FIRE. ePrint 2021/1351 was unobtainable (403 from four routes) and its body was NOT summarised; the verdict rests on its abstract plus Bernstein's Appendix A.4, read in full, which analyses the claim as conditional on UNLIMITED-SAMPLE MLWE and locates the gap in the many-ciphertexts-per-one-key case -- this campaign's exact mechanism. Bernstein gives Kyber-specific ASYMPTOTIC constants (0.54668 at eta=2) and NO ML-KEM bit figure; its footnote 19 states the concrete question is 'not addressed by this paper's asymptotics'. Corpus finding HOLDS and is SYSTEMIC: 5,582 entries carry citation_verified: read with every identifier null; 1,938 of 1,939 'no abstract extractable' entries are marked read; 7,421 of 7,809 name downloads/ paths that never existed. Novelty-check defeat measured: 'multi-target' and 'one-out-of-many' do not reach the Bernstein entry.",
    "T2_measurement": "INSTRUMENT OUTCOME, branch NEITHER, outcome invalid_measurement. The frozen 4s sensitivity gate FAILED in all four cells (shift/s 0.79, 1.09, 1.97, 3.73, signs inconsistent) because the demonstration the COORDINATOR declared has EXPECTED CONTRAST EXACTLY ZERO -- see the queue's recorded Coordinator defect D2. C3 is NOT met. P1 and P2 passed by 30-100x margins AND the frozen rule emits the identical verdict on the null arm, so those passes carry no information either.",
    "T3_conversion": "Known-answer control PASSED verbatim at delta 0.00e+00, run twice with byte-identical stdout. Finite-difference table delivered at 12 cells. THREE THINGS THE TABLE HIDES, all producer-reported: (1) re-optimising m does not move dbeta AT ALL, because estimator/lwe_primal.py cost_zeta is SEQUENTIAL -- step 2 re-optimises d at fixed beta and cannot feed back, so NO REPORTED BETA IS EVER THE ARGMIN OVER THE JOINT (beta,d) GRID; (2) beta*(c) is an integer staircase and NOT monotone, falling as c rises 3/2/3 times; (3) 0.292 is not the slope of the model that produced these beta -- RC.MATZOV's own bits-per-block is 0.2742/0.2804/0.2801, so 0.292 overstates by 4.1-6.5%. Upstream estimator anomaly A1 recorded not patched: primal_bdd(params, optimize_d=False) SILENTLY DISCARDS the kwarg."
